    `has previously been charged in court for an offence listed in section 377D(3)(a)`                                                                    IS TRUE

#ASSERT `offence under s 376AA(3)` `stepdaughter of 17`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 375(2)` `stepdaughter of 17`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 376AA(3)` `stepdaughter of 17, verified belief`
#ASSERT `offence under s 376AA(3)` `stepdaughter of 17, unverified belief`
#ASSERT `offence under s 376AA(3)` `stepdaughter of 17, previously charged`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 376AA(3)` `stepdaughter of 17, verified belief`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 376AA(3) would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of exploitative sexual penetration of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: no defence of reasonable mistaken belief that B was of or above 18 years of age (section 377D(2)); the elements of section 376AA(1) taken together."

§§ `s 377CA - the presumption of an exploitative relationship`

`stepfather` MEANS `Exploitative Relationship Facts` WITH
    `the accused is the parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                           IS TRUE
    `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                IS FALSE
    `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the minor's school or educational institution`                             IS FALSE
    `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained`                                                      IS FALSE
    `the accused is a registered medical practitioner, registered TCM practitioner or psychologist and the minor is a patient`                 IS FALSE
    `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client`                                                       IS FALSE
    `the accused is lawfully married to the minor`                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `the contrary is proved`                                                                                                                   IS FALSE

`stepfather, married to the minor` MEANS `Exploitative Relationship Facts` WITH
    `the accused is the parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                           IS TRUE
    `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                IS FALSE
    `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the minor's school or educational institution`                             IS FALSE
    `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained`                                                      IS FALSE
    `the accused is a registered medical practitioner, registered TCM practitioner or psychologist and the minor is a patient`                 IS FALSE
    `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client`                                                       IS FALSE
    `the accused is lawfully married to the minor`                                                                                             IS TRUE
    `the contrary is proved`                                                                                                                   IS FALSE

`stepfather, contrary proved` MEANS `Exploitative Relationship Facts` WITH
    `the accused is the parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                           IS TRUE
    `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                IS FALSE
    `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the minor's school or educational institution`                             IS FALSE
    `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained`                                                      IS FALSE
    `the accused is a registered medical practitioner, registered TCM practitioner or psychologist and the minor is a patient`                 IS FALSE
    `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client`                                                       IS FALSE
    `the accused is lawfully married to the minor`                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `the contrary is proved`                                                                                                                   IS TRUE

`neighbour` MEANS `Exploitative Relationship Facts` WITH
    `the accused is the parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                           IS FALSE
    `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`                                                IS FALSE
    `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the minor's school or educational institution`                             IS FALSE
    `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained`                                                      IS FALSE
    `the accused is a registered medical practitioner, registered TCM practitioner or psychologist and the minor is a patient`                 IS FALSE
    `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client`                                                       IS FALSE
    `the accused is lawfully married to the minor`                                                                                             IS FALSE
    `the contrary is proved`                                                                                                                   IS FALSE

#ASSERT `presumed exploitative within section 377CA(2)` `stepfather`
#ASSERT NOT `presumed exploitative within section 377CA(2)` `stepfather, married to the minor`
#ASSERT NOT `presumed exploitative within section 377CA(2)` `stepfather, contrary proved`
#ASSERT NOT `presumed exploitative within section 377CA(2)` `neighbour`

§§ `s 377CB - consent given under misconception`

-- s 377CB illus (a): she believes it is a procedure to extract an evil spirit - misconception as to the sexual nature of the act.
`s 377CB illus (a)` MEANS `Misconception Facts` WITH
    `the victim consented under a misconception of fact`                                                                     IS TRUE
    `the misconception is that the act is not of a sexual nature`                                                            IS TRUE
    `the misconception is that the act is not for a sexual purpose`                                                          IS FALSE
    `the misconception is as to the identity of the person doing the act`                                                    IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the misconception` IS TRUE

-- s 377CB illus (b): she believes it is treatment for a chronic disease - misconception as to the purpose.
`s 377CB illus (b)` MEANS `Misconception Facts` WITH
    `the victim consented under a misconception of fact`                                                                     IS TRUE
    `the misconception is that the act is not of a sexual nature`                                                            IS FALSE
    `the misconception is that the act is not for a sexual purpose`                                                          IS TRUE
    `the misconception is as to the identity of the person doing the act`                                                    IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the misconception` IS TRUE

-- s 377CB illus (c): she believes the imposter is her husband - misconception as to identity.
`s 377CB illus (c)` MEANS `Misconception Facts` WITH
    `the victim consented under a misconception of fact`                                                                     IS TRUE
    `the misconception is that the act is not of a sexual nature`                                                            IS FALSE
    `the misconception is that the act is not for a sexual purpose`                                                          IS FALSE
    `the misconception is as to the identity of the person doing the act`                                                    IS TRUE
    `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the misconception` IS TRUE

-- s 377CB illus (d): she believes he is an influential movie director - a misconception as to attributes, not identity.
`s 377CB illus (d)` MEANS `Misconception Facts` WITH
    `the victim consented under a misconception of fact`                                                                     IS TRUE
    `the misconception is that the act is not of a sexual nature`                                                            IS FALSE
    `the misconception is that the act is not for a sexual purpose`                                                          IS FALSE
    `the misconception is as to the identity of the person doing the act`                                                    IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the misconception` IS TRUE

-- s 377CB illus (a): "B's apparent consent is therefore not a valid consent."
#ASSERT `not a consent within section 377CB` `s 377CB illus (a)`
-- s 377CB illus (b): "B's apparent consent is therefore not a valid consent."
#ASSERT `not a consent within section 377CB` `s 377CB illus (b)`
-- s 377CB illus (c): "... is therefore not a valid consent."
#ASSERT `not a consent within section 377CB` `s 377CB illus (c)`
-- s 377CB illus (d): "B's consent is therefore a valid consent."
#ASSERT NOT `not a consent within section 377CB` `s 377CB illus (d)`

§§ `s 377BA - word or gesture intended to insult modesty`

`lewd gesture` MEANS `Insult to Modesty Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                    IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                         IS `the victim`
    `intending to insult the modesty of any person`                                                                IS TRUE
    `utters any word`                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `makes any sound`                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `makes any gesture`                                                                                            IS TRUE
    `exhibits any object`                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `intending that such word or sound will be heard, or that such gesture or object will be seen, by such person` IS TRUE
    `intrudes upon the privacy of such person`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `what was said, done or exhibited`                                                                             IS "by making an obscene gesture with your hand at her"

`muttered, not meant to be heard` MEANS `Insult to Modesty Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                    IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                         IS `the victim`
    `intending to insult the modesty of any person`                                                                IS TRUE
    `utters any word`                                                                                              IS TRUE
    `makes any sound`                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `makes any gesture`                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `exhibits any object`                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `intending that such word or sound will be heard, or that such gesture or object will be seen, by such person` IS FALSE
    `intrudes upon the privacy of such person`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `what was said, done or exhibited`                                                                             IS ""

`peeping into the bathroom` MEANS `Insult to Modesty Facts` WITH
    particulars                                                                                                    IS `the particulars`
    victim                                                                                                         IS `the victim`
    `intending to insult the modesty of any person`                                                                IS TRUE
    `utters any word`                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `makes any sound`                                                                                              IS FALSE
    `makes any gesture`                                                                                            IS FALSE
    `exhibits any object`                                                                                          IS FALSE
    `intending that such word or sound will be heard, or that such gesture or object will be seen, by such person` IS FALSE
    `intrudes upon the privacy of such person`                                                                     IS TRUE
    `what was said, done or exhibited`                                                                             IS "by peeping at her through the ventilation window of her bathroom"

#ASSERT `offence under s 377BA` `lewd gesture`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 377BA` `lewd gesture`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did, intending to insult the modesty of one Lim Mei Ling, utter words, make sounds or gestures, or exhibit an object, intending that they be heard or seen by the said Lim Mei Ling, to wit, by making an obscene gesture with your hand at her, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 377BA of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 377BA` `muttered, not meant to be heard`
#ASSERT `offence under s 377BA` `peeping into the bathroom`
